// knock.fm: knock from the end gas's history (fuel.model 1): Livengood and Wu's integral over Douaud and Eyzat's delay.
//
// The end gas is the charge the flame has not reached yet. Squeezed by the piston and then by the burning gas behind
// the flame, it heats, and its chemistry runs towards lighting on its own; when it does before the flame arrives, the
// rest of it burns at once: a knock, a pressure wave that rings the chamber (the ping), as hard as the unburned share
// that lights. How near it is to that is Livengood and Wu's integral (1955) of dt / tau over its history from the
// intake valve's closing, tau its ignition delay at its pressure and temperature then: it lights when the integral
// reaches 1. Tau is Douaud and Eyzat's fit (1978, SAE 780080, from knocking engines on primary reference fuels):
//
//     tau = 17.68 ms (ON / 100)^3.402 (p / 1 atm)^-1.7 exp(3800 K / T)
//
// ON the fuel's octane index (fuels.fm). The end gas's temperature is the charge's at the valve's closing (less what
// its evaporating fuel takes, mixture.fm), squeezed isentropically (gamma 4/3, judgement for a fuel and air mixture) by
// the cylinder's own pressure since: T = T0 (p / p0)^0.25. So boost (p), spark advance (the burn's pressure earlier,
// at a smaller volume), hotter air (T0), a higher compression and a lower octane each bring it sooner, through one
// rule. The integral reaching 1 before the spark is pre-ignition.
//
// Cost: a tick is three table reads and a few multiplies (no transcendental function: the tables below hold the
// power and the exponential, written by knock_tables.py); the caller ticks every few samples, from the valve's
// closing to the burn's end, with the seconds since the last tick. Douaud and Eyzat fitted octane numbers 80 to 100:
// above 100 their power is extrapolated.
//
// What it leaves out: the low-temperature chemistry's two-stage ignition (the negative temperature coefficient
// region; the fit is one Arrhenius line), the end gas's heat loss to the walls, hot spots, the residual gas's effect
// on the delay, and where in the chamber the knock starts.
#pragma once

